6. Multi‑Level Governance Architecture

6.1 Global Layer: Protocol and Constraint Definition

Functions: Defines interoperability standards, ethical constraints on AI‑driven policy tuning, and maintains global parameter registry.

6.2 National Layer: Controller Tuning and Policy Implementation

Functions: Tunes control parameters to national context; administers Layer 1 payments; coordinates Layer 2 and Layer 3 infrastructure.

The Economic Stability Council (ESC). An independent body modeled on central bank independence operates the AHCES controller. Its mandate is statutory, operations transparent and auditable.

Weight‑Setting Procedure for S(t):

· The ESC proposes initial weights based on national statistical analysis (principal component or factor analysis of well‑being survey data).
· Proposed weights are subject to public consultation and legislative approval every 5 years.
· An independent Well‑Being Audit Office reviews weight choices and publishes an annual report on index performance.
· Emergency adjustments during crises require supermajority legislative approval and are time‑limited.

6.3 Local Layer: Experimentation and Validation

Functions: Operates Subjective Validation Pools; manages community meaning infrastructure; conducts rapid policy experiments.

6.4 Deep Reactivation Protocol (for t_P > t_P^{\max})

For individuals whose cumulative passivity exceeds the recoverability threshold, a separate Deep Reactivation Protocol is activated:

· Trigger: Longitudinal survey data indicates an individual (anonymously identified via statistical matching) has t_P > t_P^{\max}.
· Intervention: Offer of voluntary, intensive support including personalized coaching, mental health services, skill‑rebuilding programs, and graduated re‑engagement opportunities with strong social scaffolding.
· Funding: Budgeted separately from the main Layer 2 incentive pool to avoid diluting incentives for the general population.
· Ethical Safeguard: Participation is strictly voluntary and framed as an opportunity, not an obligation.

