7. Research Roadmap

7.1 Phase 1: Simulation and Parameter Estimation (Year 1–2)

Agent‑Based Model Development. Mesa (Python) with 10,000+ agents; each agent has SDT‑derived utility weights, reputation state \mu_i, and atrophy counter t_P. Controller module tunes \rho and \mu_{sys} based on aggregate statistics.

Hypotheses to Test:

· H1: With \lambda = 0, reputation Gini coefficient increases monotonically.
· H2: With \phi > 0, reactivation cost grows exponentially with t_P.
· H3: PI controller eliminates steady‑state stability error; proportional‑only does not.
· H4: Resource constraint binds during shocks; anti‑windup prevents violation.

Empirical Parameter Estimation. Reputation decay \lambda from citation half‑life; atrophy rates \phi, \psi from unemployment scarring literature; innovation elasticities from cross‑country panel data.

7.2 Phase 2: Field Pilots with Explicit Layer 3 Components (Year 3–5)

Randomized controlled trials adding meaning‑infrastructure interventions to existing cash‑transfer programs, with metrics tracking SDT need satisfaction, community engagement, creative output, and well‑being.

7.3 Phase 3: Full AHCES Implementation (Year 5–10)

Gradual expansion from local to national scale, with continuous monitoring and parameter recalibration.

